The Phone and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a> apps didn't get as many new features as some of Apple's other apps, but there are a handful of capabilities that add utility and convenience.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/iOS-27-All-the-New-Phone-and-FaceTime-Features.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1057915" /><br/>
<h2 id="phone_app">Phone App</h2><br/>
The Phone app has one major update, and that's Call Context. When you call a company, the Phone app can surface relevant information from the Mail app.<br/>
<br/>
If you call an airline, it might show your confirmation code for an upcoming flight, or your reservation code if you're calling a hotel. It doesn't listen to what you're saying, but instead looks at the number you're calling and links it to details in the Mail app.<br/>
<br/>
Call Context is an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> feature that runs entirely on-device, and it requires an iPhone 15 Pro or newer. It also works when you make a phone call from your <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> or Mac.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="facetime">FaceTime</h2><br/>
&zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; has a couple of new features, but the biggest is Dual Capture. On the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a> models and the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a>, you can use the front and back cameras at the same time while on a &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; call.<br/>
<br/>
The person you're calling is able to see your face and what's shown through the back camera.<br/>
<br/>
You can turn on Dual Capture on a supported iPhone by tapping on the camera flip button. If you only want to show the back camera feed, you can tap to turn off the front camera view.<br/>
<br/>
While streaming video with Dual Capture is limited to the &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj;, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17-pro/">iPhone 17 Pro</a>, &zwnj;iPhone 17 Pro&zwnj; Max, &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj;, and newer, anyone running <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> can see a dual video stream on a &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; call because there are no hardware requirements for the receiving device.<br/>
<br/>
There are a few other features worth knowing about:<br/>
<ul><br/>
 <li><strong>Connection Quality</strong> - When you have a bad connection, &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; calls will now have better quality than before.</li><br/>
 <li><strong>Wi-Fi/Cellular</strong> - In &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, iPhones are better at transitioning from a Wi-Fi to a cellular connection and vice versa, so you'll lose connection less often when moving between networks.</li><br/>
 <li><strong>Live Captions</strong> - Live Captions are now available in Traditional Chinese.</li><br/>
 <li><strong>Communication Safety</strong> - Communication Safety blocks gore and violence in &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; and Messages instead of just nudity.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<h2 id="ios_27_launch">iOS 27 Launch</h2><br/>
&zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; is being beta tested right now, and can be downloaded by developers and public beta testers. It will launch this fall alongside new iPhone models.<br/>
